{
  "version": 1,
  "title": "Latency, explained (illustrated)",
  "format": "landscape",
  "style": "pop",
  "voiceover": true,
  "voice": "en_US-bryce-medium",
  "captions": true,
  "scenes": [
    {
      "id": "hook",
      "chapter": "What is latency?",
      "narration": "You tap a button, and nothing happens. Then, a moment later, the page jumps to life. That pause is called latency: the time it takes for data to travel from you to a server and back.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "type": "image",
          "name": "gen/latency/button",
          "x": 22,
          "y": 50,
          "w": 46,
          "draw": 1.6,
          "at": "tap",
          "id": "you"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "x": 50,
          "y": 12,
          "size": 13,
          "text": "Latency",
          "draw": 0.8,
          "color": "#1e6fd9",
          "at": "latency"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "name": "gen/latency/server",
          "x": 78,
          "y": 50,
          "w": 40,
          "draw": 0.8,
          "at": "data",
          "id": "server",
          "reveal": "fade"
        },
        {
          "type": "arrow",
          "from": "you",
          "to": "server",
          "bend": 8,
          "label": "request",
          "color": "#1e6fd9",
          "draw": 0.6,
          "at": "travel"
        },
        {
          "type": "arrow",
          "from": "server",
          "to": "you",
          "bend": 8,
          "label": "response",
          "color": "#2a9d4b",
          "draw": 0.6,
          "at": "back"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "x": 50,
          "y": 90,
          "size": 5,
          "text": "the time for one round trip: there and back",
          "draw": 1,
          "color": "#6b6b6b",
          "at": "time"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "bandwidth",
      "narration": "People often mix up latency and bandwidth. Bandwidth is how much data can flow at once, like the number of lanes on a highway. Latency is how long a single trip takes, like the length of the road.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "x": 50,
          "y": 9,
          "size": 8,
          "text": "Bandwidth is not latency",
          "draw": 0.8,
          "at": "mix"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "name": "gen/latency/highway",
          "x": 28,
          "y": 48,
          "w": 48,
          "draw": 1.0,
          "at": "bandwidth#2",
          "reveal": "fade"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "x": 28,
          "y": 84,
          "size": 5.5,
          "text": "bandwidth = the lanes",
          "draw": 0.6,
          "color": "#1e6fd9",
          "at": "lanes"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "name": "gen/latency/road",
          "x": 72,
          "y": 48,
          "w": 48,
          "draw": 2.5,
          "at": "latency#2"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "x": 72,
          "y": 84,
          "size": 5.5,
          "text": "latency = the length of the road",
          "draw": 0.8,
          "color": "#c0392b",
          "at": "length"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "distance",
      "chapter": "Where the time goes",
      "narration": "The first cause is distance. Light in a fibre cable covers about two hundred kilometres every millisecond. So a trip from London to New York and back takes at least fifty six milliseconds, before anything else happens.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "x": 50,
          "y": 9,
          "size": 8,
          "text": "Cause 1: distance",
          "draw": 0.8,
          "at": "first"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "name": "gen/latency/distance",
          "x": 30,
          "y": 54,
          "w": 56,
          "draw": 1.8,
          "at": "distance"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "x": 72,
          "y": 38,
          "size": 5,
          "text": "light in fibre: about 200 km every ms",
          "draw": 1,
          "at": "light"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "x": 72,
          "y": 54,
          "size": 5,
          "text": "London to New York and back",
          "draw": 0.8,
          "at": "london"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "x": 72,
          "y": 67,
          "size": 9,
          "text": "at least 56 ms",
          "draw": 0.8,
          "color": "#c0392b",
          "at": "fifty six"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "hops",
      "narration": "The second cause is hops. Your data passes through many routers on the way. Each one reads the packet, decides where it goes next, and sometimes makes it wait in a queue.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "x": 50,
          "y": 9,
          "size": 8,
          "text": "Cause 2: hops",
          "draw": 0.8,
          "at": "second"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "name": "gen/latency/routers",
          "x": 34,
          "y": 52,
          "w": 62,
          "draw": 3.0,
          "at": "routers"
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "x": 62,
          "y": 40,
          "size": 5,
          "items": [
            "reads the packet",
            "decides where it goes next",
            "may wait in a queue"
          ],
          "draw": 1.6,
          "at": "reads"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "trips",
      "narration": "The third cause is round trips. Before a secure page even starts loading, your browser and the server trade several messages: a DNS lookup, a TCP handshake and a TLS handshake. Every one of them is a full trip.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "x": 50,
          "y": 9,
          "size": 8,
          "text": "Cause 3: round trips",
          "draw": 0.8,
          "at": "third"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "id": "rt",
          "x": 63,
          "y": 52,
          "w": 90,
          "size": 5,
          "title": "Before the first byte (London to New York)",
          "rows": [
            [
              "Step",
              "Trips",
              "Time"
            ],
            [
              "DNS lookup",
              "1",
              "56 ms"
            ],
            [
              "TCP handshake",
              "1",
              "56 ms"
            ],
            [
              "TLS handshake",
              "1",
              "56 ms"
            ],
            [
              "Request the page",
              "1",
              "56 ms"
            ],
            [
              "Total",
              "4",
              "224 ms"
            ]
          ],
          "draw": 1.0,
          "at": "secure",
          "rowGap": 0.15
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "name": "gen/latency/handshake",
          "x": 21,
          "y": 55,
          "w": 40,
          "draw": 2.6,
          "at": "handshake"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "x": 63,
          "y": 90,
          "size": 5,
          "text": "every one is a full trip",
          "draw": 0.8,
          "color": "#c0392b",
          "at": "every"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "server",
      "narration": "Finally, the server needs time to think. It reads from the database, runs your code and builds the page. A single slow query here can cost more than all the travel combined.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "x": 50,
          "y": 9,
          "size": 8,
          "text": "Cause 4: server time",
          "draw": 0.8,
          "at": "finally"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "name": "gen/latency/database",
          "x": 28,
          "y": 54,
          "w": 50,
          "draw": 2.0,
          "at": "database"
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "x": 56,
          "y": 38,
          "size": 5,
          "items": [
            "reads from the database",
            "runs your code",
            "builds the page"
          ],
          "draw": 1.6,
          "at": "reads"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "x": 64,
          "y": 80,
          "size": 4.5,
          "text": "one slow query can cost more than all the travel",
          "draw": 1,
          "color": "#c0392b",
          "at": "slow"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "numbers",
      "chapter": "Numbers to know",
      "narration": "Here is a sense of scale. Reading from memory takes about a tenth of a microsecond. A round trip inside a data centre takes half a millisecond. A continent away, about forty milliseconds. An ocean away, well over a hundred.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "x": 50,
          "y": 9,
          "size": 8,
          "text": "A sense of scale",
          "draw": 0.8,
          "at": "here"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "name": "gen/latency/memory",
          "x": 17,
          "y": 52,
          "w": 30,
          "draw": 1.5,
          "at": "scale"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "id": "nums",
          "x": 60,
          "y": 52,
          "w": 90,
          "size": 5.5,
          "rows": [
            [
              "Operation",
              "Typical time"
            ],
            [
              "Read from memory",
              "0.0001 ms"
            ],
            [
              "Round trip in a data centre",
              "0.5 ms"
            ],
            [
              "A continent away",
              "40 ms"
            ],
            [
              "An ocean away",
              "150 ms"
            ]
          ],
          "draw": 1.0,
          "at": "memory",
          "rowGap": 0.15
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "feel",
      "narration": "And people feel it. Under a tenth of a second feels instant. At around one second, people notice the wait. After about ten seconds, many of them simply leave.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "x": 50,
          "y": 9,
          "size": 8,
          "text": "People feel it",
          "draw": 0.8,
          "at": "feel"
        },
        {
          "type": "line",
          "x1": 8,
          "y1": 62,
          "x2": 60,
          "y2": 62,
          "draw": 0.6,
          "at": "under"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "x": 12,
          "y": 54,
          "size": 6,
          "text": "0.1 s",
          "draw": 0.4,
          "color": "#2a9d4b",
          "at": "tenth"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "x": 12,
          "y": 70,
          "size": 4.5,
          "text": "feels instant",
          "draw": 0.5,
          "at": "instant"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "x": 34,
          "y": 54,
          "size": 6,
          "text": "1 s",
          "draw": 0.4,
          "color": "#1e6fd9",
          "at": "one"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "x": 34,
          "y": 70,
          "size": 4.5,
          "text": "people notice",
          "draw": 0.5,
          "at": "notice"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "x": 56,
          "y": 54,
          "size": 6,
          "text": "10 s",
          "draw": 0.4,
          "color": "#c0392b",
          "at": "ten"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "x": 56,
          "y": 70,
          "size": 4.5,
          "text": "many leave",
          "draw": 0.5,
          "at": "many"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "name": "gen/latency/leave",
          "x": 80,
          "y": 54,
          "w": 44,
          "draw": 2.0,
          "at": "after"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cdn",
      "chapter": "How to cut it",
      "narration": "So how do we cut latency? First, move the data closer. A content delivery network keeps copies of a site on servers around the world, so your request travels a few hundred kilometres instead of crossing an ocean.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "x": 50,
          "y": 9,
          "size": 8,
          "text": "Fix 1: move the data closer",
          "draw": 0.8,
          "at": "closer"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "name": "gen/latency/content-delivery-network",
          "x": 38,
          "y": 54,
          "w": 64,
          "draw": 1.2,
          "at": "content delivery network",
          "reveal": "fade"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "x": 80,
          "y": 44,
          "size": 5,
          "text": "a few hundred km: about 5 ms",
          "draw": 0.8,
          "color": "#2a9d4b",
          "at": "few hundred"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "x": 80,
          "y": 60,
          "size": 5,
          "text": "across an ocean: 56 ms or more",
          "draw": 0.8,
          "color": "#c0392b",
          "at": "ocean"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "fewer",
      "narration": "Second, make fewer trips. Keep connections open so you only shake hands once, use newer protocols like HTTP 3 that need fewer round trips, and cache answers so the next request never leaves the device.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "x": 50,
          "y": 9,
          "size": 8,
          "text": "Fix 2: make fewer trips",
          "draw": 0.8,
          "at": "fewer"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "name": "gen/latency/handshake",
          "x": 20,
          "y": 52,
          "w": 36,
          "draw": 2.4,
          "at": "connections"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "id": "rt2",
          "x": 64,
          "y": 48,
          "w": 70,
          "size": 5,
          "title": "Trips before the page",
          "rows": [
            [
              "Connection",
              "Trips"
            ],
            [
              "New (TCP + TLS 1.3)",
              "3"
            ],
            [
              "HTTP/3",
              "2"
            ],
            [
